ant  text message that will pertain to the  ending it says the word surprise but  we'll get to that in a bit on her way  down from the Attic she senses him there  and throws a bucket of paint which  actually is a great cool jump scare and  damn James is gonna be super pissed when  he finds this mess coming home and what  happens next is one of my favorite  scenes in the film as Cecilia tries to  fend off the Invisible Man and what  makes it so visceral is that it actually  feels like she's fighting an invisible  man unlike a lot of other films where it  just looks like the actor is fighting  air this is in part to having an actual  actor in a green suit play the attacker  so when Cecilia is hitting him it's  actually hitting someone the hits feel  like they're actually landing and not  just stopping in midair  cecilia manages to escape and calls a  lift someplace very far away Adrian's  home to look for proof that she's not  crazy one of the things I love about her  return is that all the furniture has  been covered up in linen so you're never  quite sure what could pop out and get  her it makes for a very uneasy sequence  in the basement we find Adrian's lab he  was the founder of a company called  optics which specialised in optical tech  it's here Cecilia finds the suit that  allows them to be invisible whereas  previous incarnations of the Invisible  Man were more biological in nature the  20/20 version is more grounded in  reality with writer director Leigh  Whannell actually telling reporters that  during his research on the project this  type of suit is theoretically possible  it's also interesting to note that a  suit that manipulates light in order to  achieve invisibility was created by a  man who uses manipulation to control  Cecilia the light of his life Cecilia  takes the suit and hides it in the same  hidden compartment she used for her  initial escape when she is once again  attacked by Adrian and Adrian is pretty  bad at this whole attack a defensele